What is the value of $x^2 + y^2 + z^2$ if $x^2 y + y^2 z + z^2 x = 2186$ and $xy^2 + yz^2 + zx^2 = 2188$ for integers $x, y, z$? 

Given: 
\begin{align*}
x^2 y + y^2 z + z^2 x &= 2186 \quad \text{(1)} \\
xy^2 + yz^2 + zx^2 &= 2188 \quad \text{(2)}
\end{align*}

We can manipulate the equations as follows:
\begin{align*}
(x^2 y + y^2 z + z^2 x) + (xy^2 + yz^2 + zx^2) &= 2186 + 2188 \\
(x + y + z)(xy + yz + zx) - 3xyz &= 4374 \quad \text{(3)}
\end{align*}

Subtracting equation (1) from equation (2):
\begin{align*}
xy(x - y) + yz(y - z) + zx(z - x) &= 2188 - 2186 \\
(x - y)(y - z)(z - x) &= -2 \quad \text{(4)}
\end{align*}

Now, we need to find $x, y, z$ such that equations (3) and (4) hold.

